        "width": 908,
        "height": 1162,
        "content": "# No-show handler: confirm, reschedule or cancel a meeting by email\n\nPut three buttons in your meeting reminder email and let guests confirm, reschedule or cancel with one click. Each button hits the same webhook with a different action, and the workflow updates your Google Calendar and emails the guest back. Cuts down no-shows without anyone chasing replies.\n\n### How it works\n1. A webhook receives the click. The link carries the action, the guest email, the event ID, and for reschedules a new time.\n2. A switch routes to one of three branches based on that action.\n3. Confirm: the event is fetched by ID, the guest email and Google Meet link are read from it, and a confirmation email is sent.\n4. Reschedule: an AI agent reads the requested time, creates a replacement event with Google Meet enabled, then deletes the original. The guest is emailed the new time and link.\n5. Cancel: the event is fetched, deleted from the calendar, and a cancellation email is sent.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Google Calendar and Gmail accounts, and add your OpenAI API key.\n2. Replace YOUR_CALENDAR_ID on all five calendar nodes with the calendar these meetings live in.\n3. Replace YOUR_TIMEZONE in the agent prompt and the create event tool with your own timezone, for example Europe/London.\n4. Activate, then build your reminder email links as the webhook URL plus action, email, eventId and newDateTime as query parameters.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the three email bodies to match your branding, or change the new event title in the create event tool."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
